     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the normal per-dose range of 500\u20131,000 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **A different dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg two or three times daily.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is really what you intend, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
